  - Implement net indent calculation comparing demand against unreserved warehouse stock.
  - Deliver screen STR-01 (Indent and Surplus Reuse Gate).
  - Acceptance Test: Net indent correctly flags surplus allocations and blocks duplicate raw material purchases.

* STORY-05.2: Supplier PO & ASN Tracking (S10)
  - Implement S10 schema: supplier_po, supplier_po_line, asn, vendor_scorecard.
  - Deliver screens SRC-01 (Supplier PO / Approval) and SRC-02 (Vendor ETA and Shortage Risk).
  - Acceptance Test: Inbound delivery delays dynamically trigger shortage warnings in dependent cut orders.

[EPIC-06] Raw Material Inventory Ledger & Metrology (S11, S12)
Goal: Track fabric roll lifecycle with append-only ledger movements, 4-point metrology, and double-witness issuances.

* STORY-06.1: Append-Only Material Movement Ledger (S11)
  - Implement S11 schema: inventory_location, stock_lot, fabric_roll, stock_movement.
  - Enforce conservation: stock can never be updated in-place; all adjustments require signed movement records.
  - Deliver screen STR-03 (Live Stores and Roll Location Map).
  - Acceptance Test: A17 (Prohibit consuming the same reserved fabric roll across multiple cut plans).

* STORY-06.2: Fabric Inspection Metrology & Defect Coordinate Mapping (S12)
  - Implement 4-point fabric inspection capture: length, usable width, shade band, and calibrated 2D defect coordinates.
  - Deliver screens STR-02 (Gate Intake and Fabric Inspection) and STR-07 (Shade and Roll Grading).
  - Acceptance Test: A16 (Capture actual physical roll dimensions from metrology; reject uncalibrated reads).

* STORY-06.3: Double-Witness Material Custody Transfer (S11)
  - Implement HMAC-SHA256 authenticated roll issue requiring distinct storekeeper and cutting receiver digital IDs.
  - Deliver screen STR-04 (Double-Witness Material Issue Station).
  - Acceptance Test: A19 (Issue and return require two authenticated witnesses; generate immutable custody record).

[EPIC-07] Cut Plan Optimization, Lay Execution & Bundle Commissioning (S13)
Goal: Execute physical cutting, record actual ply layups, evaluate end-bit dispositions, and bind physical tags to bundles.

* STORY-07.1: Marker Yield & End-Bit Disposition Calculator (S13)
  - Implement lay tracking: order, cut number, roll ID, lay range (max 210 plies), and residual fabric threshold classification (<1.5m scrap, 1.5–5.0m recut-hold, >5.0m store-return).
  - Deliver screen CUT-01 (Cut Plan Optimizer) and CUT-02 (Spreading and Cutting Execution).
  - Acceptance Test: A18 (Cut plies differing from planned generate actual physical piece counts, not planned numbers).

* STORY-07.2: Component Bundle Numbering & Reusable Tag Binding (S13)
  - Implement 1..N sequential bundle generator across plies, pant positions, and component parts.
  - Bind reusable HF/NFC tags with strict non-overlapping interval constraints via PostgreSQL exclusion indexes.
  - Deliver screens CUT-03 (Post-Cut Numbering) and CUT-04 (Bundle Commissioning HMI).
  - Acceptance Test: A11 (Retire reusable tag binding only after bundle lifecycle completion; prevent alias collisions).

