PHASE 3: SHOP-FLOOR SEWING EXECUTION, QUALITY & WORKFORCE (S14–S17, S23)
================================================================================

[EPIC-08] Station Edge Kernel & Local Offline Operation
Goal: Deploy a hardened, deterministic runtime at workstations to debounce readers, enforce dwell, and buffer transactions offline.

* STORY-08.1: Embedded Gateway Architecture & Local SQLite WAL Outbox
  - Package Go station daemon with local SQLite WAL store-and-forward outbox.
  - Synchronize clock offsets, monotonic intervals, and cryptographic gateway timestamps.
  - Acceptance Test: A32 (8-hour WAN isolation retains all accepted events; replays without duplication upon reconnect).

* STORY-08.2: Station HMI, Physical Reader Debounce & Evidence Evaluation
  - Implement zero-typing HMI: deliberate HF IN/OUT pads, large button controls, multi-lingual audio guidance.
  - Enforce anti-ghost-tap dwell floors (40% of SAM) and evidence policy classification (E0–E4).
  - Deliver screens SEW-01 (Sewing Station HMI) and SEW-06 (My Next Bundle).
  - Acceptance Test: A13 & A14 (Deduplicate 100 repeated taps; reject cycle completions violating dwell floor).

[EPIC-09] Line Execution, Carrier Lineage & Assembly Merging (S14)
Goal: Enforce assembly DAG constraints, validate part marriage rules, and record operator piece credits.

* STORY-09.1: Carrier State Machine & Atomic Assembly Merging (S14)
  - Implement S14 schema: carrier, carrier_parent, work_claim, accepted_operation_credit.
  - Enforce marriage checks: verify identical cut number, pant position, and ply ranges before allowing bundle joins.
  - Acceptance Test: A09 & A34 (Reject cross-cut/cross-shade assembly; prevent double-spending parent bundles in races).

* STORY-09.2: Line Bottleneck Tracking & Execution Management (S14)
  - Implement real-time queue age tracking, starvation/blockage detection, and hourly line pace calculations.
  - Deliver screens SEW-03 (Line Execution Console) and LIN-01 (Operation Bottleneck Map).
  - Acceptance Test: Station latency and bottleneck deviations exceeding 15% immediately flag supervisory alerts.

[EPIC-10] Multi-Tier Quality Inspection, NCR & Defect Tracking (S17)
Goal: Capture inline defects, manage rework queues, and enforce statistical AQL lot acceptance.

* STORY-10.1: Inline Quality Capture & Rework Dispatch (S17)
  - Implement S17 schema: inspection, inspection_finding, defect_code, rework_ticket.
  - Segregate defective units into rework loops without creating phantom units or cycles in the master route DAG.
  - Deliver screens SEW-02 (Inline QC), QS-02 (Live Defect Feed), and QS-04 (Repair Queue).
  - Acceptance Test: A20 & A21 (Quarantine failed units; ensure repaired units undergo fresh verification).

* STORY-10.2: Statistical AQL Audit & Multi-Line Quality Governance (S17)
  - Implement AQL sampling tables, inspection dispositions (Release, Rework, Scrap), and Defect Pareto analytics.
  - Deliver screens QS-01 (Line Quality Dashboard), QM-01 (Plant Quality Overview), and QLT-01 (Quarantine & NCR).
  - Acceptance Test: A28 (Failed AQL lot audit halts packing carton release and downstream shipping release).

[EPIC-11] Workforce Allocation, Skills & Maintenance Dispatch (S15, S16, S23)
Goal: Govern operator line balancing, machine availability, and unified no-blame issue escalation.

* STORY-11.1: Skill-Matrix Roster & Absence Balancing (S15)
  - Implement S15 schema: workers, skills, certifications, attendance_register, line_assignments.
  - Deliver screens LIN-02 (Labor/Float Assignment) and PM-04 (Workforce & Attendance Radar).
  - Acceptance Test: A38 (Simulating absent critical skill triggers infeasibility alert and suggests certified floats).

* STORY-11.2: Machine Asset Maintenance & Telemetry Tracking (S16)
  - Implement machine roster, breakdown logging, maintenance work orders, and spare parts inventory tracking.
  - Deliver screens SEW-04 (Mechanic Ticket Terminal) and MNT-01 (Preventive Maintenance Plan).
  - Acceptance Test: Machine breakdown auto-trips line rebalancing alerts and logs downtime to line metrics.

* STORY-11.3: Unified No-Blame Issue Coordination Mesh (S23)
  - Implement plant-wide issue escalation bus: issue ID, severity, line/station scope, owner, watchers, action log.
  - Deliver screen PM-02 (Live Issues Situation Room).
  - Acceptance Test: Issue raised on station HMI appears simultaneously on line supervisor and plant manager consoles.

